 [{:id :N1 :priority :P1 :relates-to :F1
   :anchor "cmd/govone-dev/s6a_fixture_test.go:630-667,711-729"
   :problem "The signed-deny assertion accepts 503 GOV_INFER_0003/capacity_unavailable plus a failed route projection. This does not distinguish the intended no-local-candidate branch from a genuine unrelated capacity-check failure. A previous allow success, absence of active local endpoints from an earlier API list, and a separate dry-run active deny do not establish that this specific completion reached the intended no_local_endpoints branch. An endpoint-store read error during the deny completion can produce exactly the accepted envelope and failed route while a regression in completion policy evaluation would otherwise have allowed external dispatch."
   :source-causality ["internal/inference/service.go:1065-1081 evaluates the policy then calls measuredLocalCapacity; :1672-1680 returns checker errors."
                      "internal/router/service.go:112-131 maps an endpoint store ListModelEndpoints error to capacity.ErrUnavailable, whereas the desired no_local_endpoints result is a distinct successful checker return."
                      "internal/inference/service.go:1085-1096 can intentionally convert that successful no_local_endpoints result to capacity.ErrUnavailable when local-only resolves with hypothetical local capacity and does not resolve without it; policy/service.go:541-553 makes this a plausible signed-deny branch."
                      "internal/inference/service.go:1098-1117 emits the same 503 GOV_INFER_0003 reason capacity_unavailable and failed route audit for remaining capacity errors; :2216-2229,2285-2291 projects no discriminating capacity-failure cause. internal/goverror/error.go:310-313 permits only the broad reason. Thus the expected 503 is source-plausible but not uniquely attributable by the asserted evidence."]
   :minimal-fix "Do not count this 503 alone as the signed-policy/cache negative. Implement a source-supported discriminating control/oracle within the one-file grant that demonstrates the request's deny decision separately from unrelated capacity errors, or require the 403 branch when feasible and fail/record the 503 as inconclusive. If no existing authorized seam can distinguish these paths, preserve the precise owner observability gap and seek an explicit scope decision; do not label capacity as policy denial or claim warm-cache denial from the ambiguous 503. An allow-after-deny control can add confidence but cannot by itself exclude a transient failure during the denial request."
   :future-oracle "Under separately authorized execution, an injected/transient endpoint-list failure at the deny request must not pass as evidence that the signed deny stopped egress; the genuine no-local case must be identified by discriminating evidence or reported as inconclusive, with zero captures and no generic-success promotion."}]
